Package: terrio
Type: Package
Title: Native Rust Vector I/O for R Without GDAL (Prototype)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Egor", "Kotov", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "kotov.egor@gmail.com")
Description: Native R bindings for the Terrio geospatial library (a pure-Rust
    engine, without a GDAL runtime dependency). Reads GeoPackage, GeoJSON,
    Shapefile, FlatGeobuf and GeoParquet layers into a standalone data
    representation that keeps attributes, WKB geometries and CRS metadata;
    lists layers; converts to and from 'sf'; and writes vectors. Thin
    bindings: drivers, CRS handling and algorithms stay in the Terrio Rust
    library, pinned to its published crates.io release.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/e-kotov/terrio
BugReports: https://github.com/e-kotov/terrio/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Imports: utils
Suggests:
    sf,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    wk
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.90
